= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [The Union of Soviet Socialist Republics (USSR) came into existence following the Bolshevik Revolution of 1917 under the leadership of which historic figure?], (
  [Joseph Stalin], [Vladimir Lenin], [Leon Trotsky], [Nikita Khrushchev],
))

#mcq(2, [In which year did the historic fall of the Berlin Wall take place, symbolizing the collapse of the Cold War division in Europe?], (
  [1985], [1989], [1990], [1991],
))

#mcq(3, [Which two reformist policies were introduced by Mikhail Gorbachev after becoming General Secretary of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union in 1985?], (
  [Collectivisation and Industrialisation], [Perestroika and Glasnost], [New Economic Policy and Comintern], [Shock Therapy and Open Door Policy],
))

#mcq(4, [In December 1991, which three key Slavic republics under Boris Yeltsin's leadership formally declared the dissolution of the Soviet Union?], (
  [Russia, Kazakhstan, and Uzbekistan], [Russia, Ukraine, and Belarus], [Russia, Georgia, and Armenia], [Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania],
))

#mcq(5, [Which of the following former Soviet republics completely refused to join the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) and instead joined NATO and the EU in 2004?], (
  [Central Asian Republics], [Caucasian Republics], [The Three Baltic Republics], [Belarus and Ukraine],
))

#mcq(6, [The painful process of rapid transition from a planned socialist economy to free-market capitalism sponsored by the IMF and World Bank was known as:], (
  [Democratic Socialism], [Perestroika], [Shock Therapy], [Structural Hegemony],
))

#mcq(7, [The large-scale, undervalued auctioning of roughly 90% of state-owned industries in post-Soviet Russia was popularly characterized as:], (
  [The Great Leap Forward], [The Largest Garage Sale in History], [The New Deal], [The Marshall Plan of the East],
))

#mcq(8, [The peaceful and democratic split of Czechoslovakia into the Czech Republic and Slovakia in January 1993 is historically remembered as the:], (
  [Balkan Tragedy], [Prague Spring], [Velvet Divorce], [Orange Revolution],
))

#mcq(9, [Tajikistan in Central Asia witnessed a devastating civil war following the collapse of the USSR that lasted for how many years?], (
  [3 years], [5 years], [10 years], [15 years],
))

#mcq(10, [The supersonic cruise missile 'BrahMos' represents a landmark defense joint venture between India and which foreign country?], (
  [United States], [France], [Israel], [Russia],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [Vladimir Lenin led the Bolshevik Revolution in Russia in October/November 1917, overthrowing the Tsarist regime and establishing the world's first socialist state, the USSR.], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [The Berlin Wall, erected in 1961, was breached and pulled down by ordinary citizens on 9 November 1989, leading to the formal reunification of Germany in October 1990.], answer: [B])

#solution(3, [Mikhail Gorbachev introduced Perestroika (economic restructuring) and Glasnost (political openness) to modernize the Soviet system, which inadvertently hastened its dissolution.], answer: [B])

#solution(4, [In December 1991, the leaders of Russia (Boris Yeltsin), Ukraine (Leonid Kravchuk), and Belarus (Stanislav Shushkevich) signed the Belavezha Accords, formally declaring the USSR dissolved.], answer: [B])

#solution(5, [The three Baltic states—Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania—were the first to secede from the USSR in 1990, rejected CIS membership, and integrated with the West by joining NATO and the EU in 2004.], answer: [C])

#solution(6, [Shock Therapy was the abrupt transition model prescribed by the International Monetary Fund and World Bank, imposing sweeping privatization and immediate price deregulation.], answer: [C])

#solution(7, [The sell-off of over 90% of Russian state industries at throwaway voucher rates was famously described as 'the largest garage sale in history', resulting in economic plunder by oligarchs.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [The amicable, bloodless partition of Czechoslovakia into the Czech Republic and Slovakia on 1 January 1993 is universally referred to by historians as the 'Velvet Divorce'.], answer: [C])

#solution(9, [Tajikistan suffered a vicious sectarian and clan civil war that lasted for 10 years, from 1991 until a comprehensive peace accord was brokered with Russian mediation in 2001.], answer: [C])

#solution(10, [BrahMos (named after the Brahmaputra and Moskva rivers) is a world-class supersonic cruise missile developed jointly by India's DRDO and Russia's NPO Mashinostroyeniya.], answer: [D])

